what's up guys it was just announced the  all-new secret lab magnus pro  desk  the first standing desk from secret lab  so many of you have been asking for this  they have finally released it i've been  testing this desk for the past couple  weeks this is the 1.7 meter version  there's also a 1.5 meter version and i'm  gonna tell you this is probably one of  my favorite standing desks in the  marketplace  except for this one thing and this one  thing what is it we'll talk about that  in just a bit but first we're going to  focus on the positives what i enjoy  about using this desk and what i like  about it so much  secret lab is still carry that dna over  from trying to keep your cables away  from your desk making sure that when you  look at your desk you don't see cables  all over the place it's clean  it's awesome to look at and that dna is  still here in this magnus pro okay and  the design element is pretty much the  same to be honest with you i mean when  you look at both of these desks beside  the size of it and looking at the legs  you probably wouldn't be able to tell  which desk is which  but  for a lot of you who are worried about  the wobble of the original magnus is  that here in the pro it's not the  standing legs are very secure could hold  up to about 125 kgs of weight on the  desk so that's pretty much good unless  people want to lay on top of it with a  partner and do some other things which  we're not going to talk about in this  video but outside of that you're going  to be more than happy with this um what  else do i like about this desk is the  design it's a little bit less gamer-ish  in my personal opinion what do i mean by  that well when i first got the magnus  desk it had this black matte sort of  magnetic you know covering to it it had  gold writing and had red stitching they  very much kind of it was kind of in your  face right well this one is a stealth  black look it's sleek it's nondescript  if you're a business person or if your  person doesn't want that sort of  bold look to your desk you're going to  really enjoy this now you still have the  rgb lighting on the back of this you are  going to see the red accents here and  there especially in the monitor which  we'll talk about in just a bit and of  course the cable management  magnetic holders for that matter but  outside of that  it is really just sleek black  utilitarian and it feels like it's a  little bit more mature in my personal  opinion okay  but let's also go to some of the  accessories on this first we've got to  talk about the elephant in the room the  monitor arm so many of you were asking  us in our videos what monitor did you  use on the magnus desk how did you get  it so sleek which is that i need to buy  it well that is a prism rx stealth  monitor arm and it fit beautifully on  the magnus and now secret lab has made  their own monitor arm very reminiscent  of that design but it's a little bit  more angular it's matte black with this  metallic red accents that we've seen  from secret lab but this monitor arm has  a p-load of around 8 kgs in weight so i  have this iso 27-inch monitor that i've  been uh borrowing from a friend of mine  ivan joshua lowe who's very kind enough  to loan me this monitor because it'll  monitors are not cheap at all  and  alone without any accessories this  monitor weighs in at 7.7 kg  now with this uh sort of covering the  side covering to reduce glare that's  going to put it around 8 kg thereabouts  this monitor arm holds it no problems at  all it is great you can turn it  vertically horizontally doesn't matter  it's fantastic of course i talked about  this matte here that's all still black  now there are different color  configurations which you've probably  already seen  and yeah some are a little bit more bold  than others but i like this one but i  think a lot of you are going to like  some of the newer accessories this pc  mount bracket that goes to the bottom  right hand side of the desk here now i  don't have that here because my desk is  powered by a macbook pro 16-inch m1 max  which is here on my desk but if you do  have a pc tower you can rig that  underneath the desk it's padded so it's  going to protect your pc tower you can  run your cables to the back of the cable  tray and you're good to go  also you have the magnetic headphone  holder which is great to have especially  for gaming and editing and all that  great stuff and i use that a lot  a lot of the accessories are  interchangeable for the most part i  don't know about the pc mount i know the  monitor arm is and of course the  headphone holder but if you have the  original magnus with those accessories  you can bring that over here to the pro  no issues at all how i have my desk set  up i mean because i need a 1.7 meter  desk because because i have the monitor  here my macbook pro logitech keyboard  here magic uh trackpad got harman kardon  speakers i've got this oc white ultima  uh mic arm here because this is how i do  my recording and my voiceover work got  the neumann tlm-107 mic here  i'm all set up right in this area this  side is relatively empty because this is  where i do a lot of my content where i  shoot a lot of my content where i'm  doing this kind of stuff right here and  also if i want to do some you know  photography of products or b-roll-on  products i will shoot it in this area  and behind me in the terrible display  case so that's sort of how i set up my  studio for the most part and that's why  i think this extra space  really helped me a lot using this desk  for the past couple weeks now unlike  other  desks out there where the controls to  move it up and down are an external  control panel this is built into the  tabletop it is very sleek it is very  awesome you have customizable buttons so  you can set different heights on this  you have an led panel so you can see the  height and measurements it's great it's  awesome i love it and it lights up as  well now we got to talk about the lights  in the back of it very reminiscent of  the original lights but now they're  controlled by nano leaf you have a  physical controller attached to the  lights also you can control by an app  and it's great flexible the same exact  design language except that physical  controller is nicer you can attach it to  your desk by a 3m tape that's included  and you don't worry about losing that  little  uh tiny controller that came with the  original magnus which i almost lost a  few times so you know this is nicer this  way i appreciate this now the cable bay  or tray  is a little different from the previous  version case in point that trap door  that was underneath on the original  magnus is no longer there secret lab  told us that a lot of people didn't use  that so they just took it out  also  it to me feels a little shallower now  secret lab says it's deeper but to me it  feels a little bit shallower if you're  having a problem  plugging in your larger power bricks  into this because you have a power strip  that's plugged into the back of it  you need to  flip or reverse that power strip inside  the cable tray that means if you have a  three prong system the two prongs are  facing the back and the front prong is  facing forward towards the desk then you  can plug these larger devices in if you  do it the other way you're not gonna get  anything in because of the the allotment  of room so keep that in mind a little  tip that i learned from secret lab  trying to set up this desk but speaking  of that bay  right there's also something else i want  to talk to you guys about and that's the  cable management on the side  and  it's a great idea to me it's a fantastic  idea but  there's something i want to show you  which makes it a little less than ideal  but i'll show you what i'm talking about  right now now on this side of the desk  you actually have a pc mount or tower  mount that you can hook up to this and  then you can actually run cables through  here and you'd be necessarily cable-free  to the you know outside world by theory  you should run the cables through here  into the cable tray  however here's the problem with this  while you can run cables here it stops  because for some reason there's just  this really small tiny opening here  which is not going to allow anything to  get through so if you have any sort of  power source anything like that you're  not going to get through that at all so  what you have to do is actually take the  cable out from there and then wrap it  around this way into the cable bay which  seems a little bit odd of a design now  case in point there are various  different sizes to let's say plugs or  whatever it may be  which could cause the secret lab to go  look maybe it's just easier to wrap it  around then they have no issues with  that at all but  if you want to make this as clutter free  and as sleek as possible  having this completely open on the  inside with a great a big opening here  to go in here into the cable tray would  have been ideal all right so  having said that let's talk about one of  the other benefits that i like about  this desk one plug goes from the bottom  of the desk the leg into the wall that  means all your power sources are plugged  into the desk itself through the power  strip that plugs into the side of the  desk there's a power outlet on the left  side the top left side  and then at the bottom left hand side  there's one cable that goes into the  wall and that's all you need to plug in  that means less wires are seen it means  it means a lot cleaner look in your room  in your studio  and to me i thought this was a genius  set up by secret lab i absolutely love  this desk my personal opinion is it's  one of the best standing desks in the  marketplace i love the sleek design i  like the accessories and i think a lot  of you out there are going to enjoy it  if there's any  uh negativity on this desk i would just  say it's the side cable management as i  mentioned earlier i wish it went all the  way into the bay without having to wrap  around but we can't have everything  right but for the most part they hit a  home run with this desk anyway those are  my thoughts on it let me know your  thoughts in the comment section below if  you like this review subscribe hit that  like button hit that notification bell  and we got a lot more great videos to  check out right here

